<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Shantong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1351">1351</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Han Shantong was a Chinese leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-lotus">White Lotus</a> sect from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> who preached the imminent coming of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maitreya">Buddha Maitreya</a> and claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> emperors. In 1351 he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-futong">Liu Futong</a> planned an uprising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>, but the plot was discovered and he was captured and executed. His followers launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-turban-rebellion">Red Turban Rebellion</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-liner">Han Lin'er</a> was proclaimed emperor of the Song in 1355.</p></div>
